sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Login with a second factor after this pull request
  accDescr: The web app posts the password to POST /login. When the user has 2FA on, the API now answers 202 with a challenge id instead of the session cookie; the TOTP form posts the 6-digit code with that id to POST /login/totp, the API checks it with the auth service's VerifyTotp and sets the session cookie only when it passes. Users without 2FA get the cookie from POST /login as before.
  participant Web as Web app
  participant API
  participant Auth as Auth service
  Web->>API: POST /login (password)
  alt 2FA on
    rect rgba(240, 83, 26, 0.14)
      API-->>Web: 202 challenge id
      Web->>API: POST /login/totp (code, challenge id)
      API->>Auth: VerifyTotp
      Auth-->>API: passes
      API-->>Web: sets session cookie
    end
  else 2FA off
    API-->>Web: sets session cookie
  end
